Matrix multiplication is more complex as it involves nested loops and requires careful management of data access patterns, which RAJA handles through its loop constructs.

### 1. Original CUDA Code (Conceptual)

A CUDA implementation would typically use a tiled approach, launching blocks to compute tiles of the resulting matrix $C$.

```c++
// cuda_matmul.cu (Conceptual Snippet)
__global__ void matmulKernel(const float* A, const float* B, float* C, int M, int N, int K) {
    // Complex indexing logic involving blockIdx, threadIdx, and tile sizes
    // ...
    C[row * N + col] += A[row * K + k] * B[k * col + col];
}
// ... launch configuration ...
