./vecadd_raja
```

> **What changed?**  
> * `RAJA::forall` replaces the manual grid/block launch.  
> * `RAJA::cuda_exec<threadsPerBlock>` tells RAJA to use a CUDA kernel with the given block size.  
> * RAJA’s memory helpers (`cuda_malloc`, `cuda_memcpy`, `cuda_free`) are thin wrappers around the CUDA runtime.  
> * The lambda is marked `__device__` just like a CUDA kernel body.

